<title>USA: Showa Denko sues ICI in patent dispute.</title>
<headline>Showa Denko sues ICI in patent dispute.</headline>
<dateline>WILMINGTON, Del 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Showa Denko KK of Japan seeks a court ruling that its products do not infringe two Imperial Chemical Industries plc patents for the manufacture of 1,1,1,2 tetrafluoroethane.</p>
<p>In papers filed Tuesday in the U.S. District Court in Delaware, the patents are described as the &quot;Manufacture of halogenated compounds&quot; and the &quot;Fluorination catalyst and process.&quot;</p>
<p>1,1,1,2 tetrafluoroethane is a replacement for freon and is used as a blowing agent and refrigerant.</p>
</text>
